> measured to five levels .
>
>
> To melt the data frame, and then split the column to reflect the question
> number_question type distinction, I do the following:
>
>
> dfm <- melt(df1, id = 1)
> dfm <- cbind(dfm[,-2], colsplit(dfm[,2], pattern="_", c("quest","type")))
>
> head(dfm)
>
>> subj value quest type
>> 1 a n q1 h
>> 2 b n q1 h
>> 3 c y q1 h
>> 4 d y q1 h
>> 5 e n q1 h
>> 6 f n q1 h
>
>
>
> What I want is a data frame that provides a contingency table of the answers
> to each question according to whether a candidate had heard of a question.
> It's like:
>
>> quest a q_1 q_1 q_1 q_1 q_1
>> 1 y # #
>> 1 n
>> 2 y
>> 2 n
>
>
>
> Where the # are the counts for that cell.
>
> Is this possible with a single dcast call?
>
> Thanks-Tom
